          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Acting humanly: Turing Test"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.165,
            0.137,
            0.916,
            0.189
          ],
          "content": "Turing (1950) \"Computing machinery and intelligence”"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.093,
            0.257,
            0.868,
            0.348
          ],
          "content": "\"Can machines think?“ \"Can machines behave intelligently?\" **Operational test for intelligent behavior: the Imitation Game**"
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.03,
            0.363,
            0.595,
            0.582
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_7_image_7.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.687,
            0.382,
            0.928,
            0.431
          ],
          "content": "**AI system passes**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.688,
            0.54,
            0.904,
            0.587
          ],
          "content": "**is the machine.**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.045,
            0.625,
            0.932,
            0.676
          ],
          "content": "**No computer vision or robotics or physical presence required!**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.054,
            0.721,
            0.907,
            0.828
          ],
          "content": "Predicted that by 2000, a machine might have a 30% chance of fooling a lay person for 5 minutes. **Achieved. (Siri!** J )"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.053,
            0.872,
            0.895,
            0.981
          ],
          "content": "But, by scientific consensus, we are still several decades away from truly passing the Turing test (as the test was intended)."
        }
      ]
    },
