          "type": "page_number",
          "bbox": [
            0.895,
            0.933,
            0.917,
            0.959
          ],
          "content": "15"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_idx": 15,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.135,
            0.063,
            0.185,
            0.104
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "So,"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.197,
            0.115,
            0.919,
            0.307
          ],
          "content": "**In near future, we can have computers with as many processing elements as our brain, but: far fewer interconnections (wires or synapses) then again, much faster updates.**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.121,
            0.369,
            0.7,
            0.468
          ],
          "content": "**Fundamentally different hardware may require fundamentally different algorithms!**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.197,
            0.477,
            0.534,
            0.519
          ],
          "content": "• **Still an open question.**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.197,
            0.529,
            0.506,
            0.569
          ],
          "content": "• **Neural net research.**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.196,
            0.581,
            0.803,
            0.625
          ],
          "content": "**Can a digital computer simulate our brain?**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.353,
            0.647,
            0.976,
            0.805
          ],
          "content": "**Likely: Church-Turing Thesis (But, might we need quantum computing?) (Penrose; consciousness; free will)**"
        },
        {
          "type": "page_number",
          "bbox": [
            0.895,
            0.933,
            0.918,
            0.959
          ],
          "content": "16"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_idx": 16,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.385,
            0.067,
            0.619,
            0.131
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "A Neuron"
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.224,
            0.848,
            0.774
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_16_image_1.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "page_number",
          "bbox": [
            0.895,
            0.933,
            0.917,
            0.959
          ],
          "content": "17"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_idx": 17,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.168,
            0.028,
            0.837,
            0.176
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "An Artificial Neural Network (Perceptrons)"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.113,
            0.296,
            0.317,
            0.35
          ],
          "content": "Output units $\\mathcal { O } _ { i }$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.115,
            0.517,
            0.317,
            0.574
          ],
          "content": "Hidden units $\\mathbf { a } _ { \\parallel }$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.117,
            0.746,
            0.313,
            0.801
          ],
          "content": "Input units $I _ { \\pm }$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.556,
            0.221,
            0.749,
            0.275
          ],
          "content": "**Output Unit**"
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.278,
            0.295,
            0.927,
            0.818
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_17_image_5.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "footer",
          "bbox": [
            0.574,
            0.889,
            0.752,
            0.94
          ],
          "content": "Input Units"
        },
        {
          "type": "page_number",
          "bbox": [
            0.895,
            0.932,
            0.917,
            0.959
          ],
          "content": "18"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_idx": 18,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.115,
            0.152,
            0.866,
            0.298
          ],
          "content": "**An artificial neural network is an abstraction (well, really, a** “**drastic simplification**”**) of a real neural network.**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.115,
            0.376,
            0.846,
            0.573
          ],
          "content": "**Start out with random connection weights on the links between units. Then train from input examples and environment, by changing network weights.**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.647,
            0.88,
            0.961
          ],
          "content": "**Recent breakthrough: Deep Learning (automatic discovery of “deep” features by a multi-layer neural network.) Deep learning is bringing perception (hearing & vision) within reach.**"
        },
        {
          "type": "page_number",
          "bbox": [
            0.895,
            0.931,
            0.918,
            0.96
          ],
          "content": "19"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_idx": 19,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.523,
            0.103,
            0.961,
            0.168
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "3. Thinking Rationally"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "bbox": [
            0.148,
            0.398,
            0.754,
            0.882
          ],
          "content": "|  | Human-like Intelligence | “Ideal” Intelligent/Rationally |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Thought/ Reasoning | Thinking humanly → Cognitive Modeling | 3. Thinking Rationally →formalizing \"Laws of Thought\" |\n| Behavior/ Actions | Acting Humanly →Turing Test | Acting Rationally |",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_19_table_1.jpg"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_idx": 20,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.39,
            0.008,
            0.962,
            0.131
          ],
          "content": "**Thinking rationally: formalizing the \"laws of thought”**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.069,
            0.134,
            0.404,
            0.188
          ],
          "content": "**Long and rich history!**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.07,
            0.197,
            0.975,
            0.319
          ],
          "content": "**Logic: Making the right inferences! Remarkably effective in science, math, and engineering.**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.07,
            0.377,
            0.874,
            0.486
          ],
          "content": "**Several Greek schools developed various forms of logic: notation and rules of derivation for thoughts.**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.07,
            0.497,
            0.897,
            0.603
          ],
          "content": "**Aristotle: what are correct arguments/thought processes? (characterization of** “**right thinking**”**).**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.37,
            0.615,
            0.63,
            0.664
          ],
          "content": "**Socrates is a man**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.037,
            0.657,
            0.2,
            0.759
          ],
          "content": "**Syllogisms Aristotle**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.372,
            0.678,
            0.654,
            0.729
          ],
          "content": "**All men are mortal**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.37,
            0.805,
            0.797,
            0.857
          ],
          "content": "**Therefore, Socrates is mortal**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.171,
            0.869,
            0.909,
            0.923
          ],
          "content": "**Can we mechanize it? (syntactic; strip interpretation)**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.172,
            0.934,
            0.758,
            0.988
          ],
          "content": "**Use: legal cases, diplomacy, ethics etc. (?)**"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_idx": 21,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.018,
            0.012,
            0.893,
            0.065
          ],
          "content": "**More contemporary logicians (e.g. Boole, Frege, and Tarski).**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.019,
            0.065,
            0.736,
            0.117
          ],
          "content": "**Ambition: Developing the “language of thought.”**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.018,
            0.118,
            0.927,
            0.172
          ],
          "content": "**Direct line through mathematics and philosophy to modern AI.**"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.019,
            0.205,
            0.228,
            0.265
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Key notion:"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.018,
            0.297,
            0.872,
            0.36
          ],
          "content": "**Inference derives new information from stored facts**."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.018,
            0.391,
            0.912,
            0.514
          ],
          "content": "Axioms can be very compact. E.g. much of mathematics can be derived (in principle) from the logical axioms of"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.127,
            0.53,
            0.681,
            0.589
          ],
          "content": "eory. Zermelo-Fraenkel with axiom of choice."
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.029,
            0.521,
            0.745,
            0.999
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_21_image_7.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.749,
            0.549,
            0.952,
            0.735
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_21_image_8.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.752,
            0.812,
            0.991,
            0.975
          ],
          "content": "**Also, Godel’s incompleteness.**"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_idx": 22,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.047,
            0.08,
            0.231,
            0.128
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Limitations:"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.095,
            0.185,
            0.821,
            0.293
          ],
          "content": "• **Not all intelligent behavior is mediated by logical deliberation (much appears not…)**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.094,
            0.346,
            0.907,
            0.61
          ],
          "content": "• **(Logical) representation of knowledge underlying intelligence is quite non-trivial. Studied in the area of “knowledge representation.” Also brings in probabilistic representations. E.g. Bayesian networks and graphical models.**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.096,
            0.665,
            0.592,
            0.715
          ],
          "content": "• **What is the purpose of thinking?**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.096,
            0.72,
            0.554,
            0.769
          ],
          "content": "• **What thoughts should I have?**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.096,
            0.812,
            0.959,
            0.861
          ],
          "content": "• **Seems to require some connection to “acting in the world.”**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.097,
            0.866,
            0.855,
            0.971
          ],
          "content": "• **We (“agents”) want/need to affect our environment (in part for survival).**"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_idx": 23,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.573,
            0.104,
            0.96,
            0.169
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "4. Acting Rationally"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "bbox": [
            0.148,
            0.398,
            0.754,
            0.882
          ],
          "content": "|  | Human-like Intelligence | “Ideal” Intelligent/Rationally |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Thought/ Reasoning | Thinking humanly → Cognitive Modeling | Thinking Rationally →formalizing \"Laws of Thought\" |\n| Behavior/ Actions | Acting Humanly →Turing Test | Acting Rationally |",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_23_table_1.jpg"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_idx": 24,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.656,
            0.015,
            0.961,
            0.079
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Rational agents"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.061,
            0.094,
            0.961,
            0.344
          ],
          "content": "**An agent is an entity that perceives and acts in the world (i.e. an “autonomous system” (e.g. self-driving cars) / physical robot or software robot (e.g. an electronic trading system))**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.099,
            0.403,
            0.866,
            0.463
          ],
          "content": "<strong><u>This course is about designing rational agents</u></strong>"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.062,
            0.528,
            0.937,
            0.685
          ],
          "content": "**For any given class of environments and tasks, we seek the agent (or class of agents) with the best performance**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.061,
            0.751,
            0.926,
            0.987
          ],
          "content": "Caveat: computational limitations may make perfect rationality unachievable àdesign **best** program for given machine resources à“Limited rationality”"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_idx": 25,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.392,
            0.07,
            0.965,
            0.142
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Building Intelligent Machines"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.045,
            0.311,
            0.964,
            0.434
          ],
          "content": "**I Building exact models of human cognition view from psychology, cognitive science, and neuroscience**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.044,
            0.492,
            0.779,
            0.783
          ],
          "content": "**II Developing methods to match or exceed human performance in certain domains, possibly by very different means Main focus of current AI.**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.086,
            0.856,
            0.924,
            0.963
          ],
          "content": "**But, I) often provides inspiration for II). Also, Neural Nets blur the separation.**"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_idx": 26,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.48,
            0.013,
            0.962,
            0.075
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Key research areas in AI"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.055,
            0.102,
            0.923,
            0.261
          ],
          "content": "**Problem solving, planning, and search --- generic problem solving architecture based on ideas from cognitive science (game playing, robotics).**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.056,
            0.273,
            0.875,
            0.378
          ],
          "content": "**Knowledge Representation – to store and manipulate information (logical and probabilistic representations)**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.054,
            0.389,
            0.942,
            0.496
          ],
          "content": "**Automated reasoning / Inference – to use the stored information to answer questions and draw new conclusions**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.054,
            0.507,
            0.923,
            0.611
          ],
          "content": "**Machine Learning – intelligence from data; to adapt to new circumstances and to detect and extrapolate patterns**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.054,
            0.623,
            0.87,
            0.726
          ],
          "content": "**Natural Language Processing – to communicate with the machine**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.054,
            0.74,
            0.78,
            0.793
          ],
          "content": "**Computer Vision --- processing visual information**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.054,
            0.805,
            0.908,
            0.909
          ],
          "content": "**Robotics --- Autonomy, manipulation, full integration of AI capabilities**"
        }
      ]
    }
